#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698430 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08cbc62b-9bae-5046-91df-3c7ad176ba5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c4/c41b8448501bcc7b43742d036593cbbf87568992697b78d3182f8da62ef11859.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698407} {:answer/id #uuid "5313a928-a6f2-58af-926b-60b41beed1ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/cc/cc8276787322388623463fd2c3e3d6120a34fbbf22ab5b46a31ea4eb939a4c6c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698414} {:answer/id #uuid "6dd0f39f-45d2-5d93-afdf-252be8cdaf2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ea/eabfc4c405a02f2b554facd96d78e4cb05ce091ca3b8756abe504fd67d2950eb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698417} {:answer/id #uuid "b1ac6765-d618-50e9-b840-73b57655cc74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/33/333900a786b4d62c04cbb270a0fd0b91e1dc64b2349806024a77c2859443161e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698428} {:answer/id #uuid "ed0f79e9-d922-5a38-94df-f9a20d8770aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a7/a74b163fdaa43a243298cfc1d6980098e0cc8db96bd0cfceb28484133c9debf9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698433}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed0f79e9-d922-5a38-94df-f9a20d8770aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a7/a74b163fdaa43a243298cfc1d6980098e0cc8db96bd0cfceb28484133c9debf9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698433} :answer-field/id #uuid "068eeff9-ad6e-5e95-aabd-7dcbb09fe37a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698406}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b9332517-42a9-5823-9757-c83156b88835" :question/problem "Determine the graph of the following parametrically defined curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x&=2 t - 1\\\\ y&=-1 + \\frac{5}{t}\\\\ &t>0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First calculate the $x$-values using $x=2 t - 1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline \\mathbf{t} & \\frac{1}{2} & 1 & 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ \\hline x & 0 & 1 & 3 & 5 & 7 \\\\ \\hline y &  &  &  &  &  \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|}\\hline \\mathbf{t} & 5 \\\\ \\hline x & 9 \\\\ \\hline y &  \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\nNow calculate $y=-1 + \\frac{5}{t}$ at the **same parameter values**:\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline \\mathbf{t} & \\frac{1}{2} & 1 & 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ \\hline x & 0 & 1 & 3 & 5 & 7 \\\\ \\hline y & 9 & 4 & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|}\\hline \\mathbf{t} & 5 \\\\ \\hline x & 9 \\\\ \\hline y & 0 \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\nPair the coordinates at the same parameter value and follow the curve only over the stated interval.\n\n![Curve through the calculated points](images/f8/f8c89c1d92cd8256446fdf43bce595b02637ba2ed74cebffea6044f8f394c61b.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698431 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "053a508d-ff09-5f51-a30f-ceb3c75605c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b6/b69aeac1f4f2d78df4253d94bff0a830414b62926c0d5177e82d18a182c5439c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698405} {:answer/id #uuid "2cb5ac91-7165-5365-ade9-a15d440a2cb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/2b/2b65d5d239952e2c3ba9c1e89e6f0c772790d029e14a02838d5135c7d484885b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698410} {:answer/id #uuid "3f90783f-2b17-5d76-bb84-69b7e3f07c1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bf/bf33cbe898c8180ea3a9df3d414d75c6832e01c2eac8db0297f32a97edcef8f2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698412} {:answer/id #uuid "4abba4c5-3c24-59c3-a13e-c4bb633bfd21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/86/86dd000dfd80e5dd212aa540949c75f46f1d32951abbec8daa708aeb8e784725.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698413} {:answer/id #uuid "f814f1a4-6c01-52fb-a5cd-c5934ef9db8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/70/7012f34740c3766043db40b5bb3caaed96c9998c6ced1a35205d000aa8ddc8c9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698436}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f814f1a4-6c01-52fb-a5cd-c5934ef9db8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/70/7012f34740c3766043db40b5bb3caaed96c9998c6ced1a35205d000aa8ddc8c9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698436} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4ce42cc-af65-566a-9fdc-a5fbcc8db4c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698429}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bc2fb875-1e69-5e14-8cf9-ca119d224218" :question/problem "Determine the graph of the following parametrically defined curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x&=5 - 2 t^{2}\\\\ y&=2 t + 2\\\\ &-1\\le t\\le 3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First calculate the $x$-values using $x=5 - 2 t^{2}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline \\mathbf{t} & -1 & 0 & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ \\hline x & 3 & 5 & 3 & -3 & -13 \\\\ \\hline y &  &  &  &  &  \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\nNow calculate $y=2 t + 2$ at the **same parameter values**:\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline \\mathbf{t} & -1 & 0 & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ \\hline x & 3 & 5 & 3 & -3 & -13 \\\\ \\hline y & 0 & 2 & 4 & 6 & 8 \\\\ \\hline\\end{array}\n$$\n\nPair the coordinates at the same parameter value and follow the curve only over the stated interval.\n\n![Curve through the calculated points](images/e0/e06b71f5c9e0f3076a8dcd534fa24ce5b319a7568e70b63f857e6150537e4ec7.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698488 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09e138e7-df53-51c6-b966-d6194c7de7da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm\\sqrt3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698476} {:answer/id #uuid "4421f56b-0f39-5807-92cd-2802a5e7c983" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\sqrt3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698478} {:answer/id #uuid "47a24d44-ca49-5c41-9253-1929bb98f2f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac{11}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698479} {:answer/id #uuid "86d295b5-e8b9-5d28-a186-12c0beeb5ddb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm\\sqrt8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698481} {:answer/id #uuid "c2d2eb5e-6539-5ef8-8322-c4fbe9720e15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698486}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09e138e7-df53-51c6-b966-d6194c7de7da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm\\sqrt3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698476} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdfd8036-aa5a-5342-9ea3-b3dfe1c40b59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698487}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cfd0bc13-62d3-5361-8096-c89ecd8ff79e" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf a=\\langle1,2,x\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf b=\\langle2,-1,x\\rangle$. Given that $|\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b|=\\sqrt{55}$, find all real values of $x$." :question/worked-solution "First compute the cross product using the determinant formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b&=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k\\\\1&2&x\\\\2&-1&x\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\n&=\\begin{vmatrix}2&x\\\\-1&x\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf i-\\begin{vmatrix}1&x\\\\2&x\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf j+\\begin{vmatrix}1&2\\\\2&-1\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf k\\\\\n&=(2x+x)\\mathbf i-(x-2x)\\mathbf j+(-1-4)\\mathbf k\\\\\n&=\\langle3x,x,-5\\rangle.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow compute its magnitude and solve the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b|&=\\sqrt{(3x)^2+x^2+(-5)^2}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{10x^2+25},\\\\\n\\sqrt{10x^2+25}&=\\sqrt{55}\\\\\n10x^2+25&=55\\\\\nx^2&=3\\\\\nx&=\\pm\\sqrt3.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor either $x=-\\sqrt3$ or $x=\\sqrt3$, the squared magnitude is $10(3)+25=55$, so both satisfy the original equation. The complete solution set is $x=\\pm\\sqrt3$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698489 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "112be27d-3377-5d5c-9a03-b5103d96382b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698477}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "112be27d-3377-5d5c-9a03-b5103d96382b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698477} :answer-field/id #uuid "06db7fad-ebe4-5019-9028-97af5258a2ce" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698475} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee922eba-5d8d-53d3-a8bb-3b2f15632360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698491}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee922eba-5d8d-53d3-a8bb-3b2f15632360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698491} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4d663fb-159b-5916-93ac-6ac3ff0d449f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698492}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d029cc23-f986-5e08-b80c-d047fc981da5" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf a=\\langle x,1,2\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf b=\\langle2,0,3\\rangle$. Given that $|\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b|=\\sqrt{38}$, find all real values of $x$.\n\nIn **ascending order**, the values are $x=$ {{field-1}} and $x=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Compute the cross product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b&=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k\\\\x&1&2\\\\2&0&3\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\n&=\\begin{vmatrix}1&2\\\\0&3\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf i-\\begin{vmatrix}x&2\\\\2&3\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf j+\\begin{vmatrix}x&1\\\\2&0\\end{vmatrix}\\mathbf k\\\\\n&=(3-0)\\mathbf i-(3x-4)\\mathbf j+(0-2)\\mathbf k\\\\\n&=\\langle3,4-3x,-2\\rangle.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIts magnitude gives a quadratic equation with a shifted square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sqrt{3^2+(4-3x)^2+(-2)^2}&=\\sqrt{38}\\\\\n13+(4-3x)^2&=38\\\\\n(4-3x)^2&=25\\\\\n4-3x&=5\\quad\\text{or}\\quad4-3x=-5\\\\\nx&=-\\frac13\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x=3.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquivalently, expanding and factoring gives $9x^2-24x-9=3(3x+1)(x-3)=0$. For $x=-\\frac13$, the cross product is $\\langle3,5,-2\\rangle$; for $x=3$, it is $\\langle3,-5,-2\\rangle$. Each has magnitude $\\sqrt{9+25+4}=\\sqrt{38}$.\n\nThus, in ascending order, the values are $-\\frac13$ and $3$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698493 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96b4fcfa-ff02-5e4f-8970-469790ed3e3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698482} {:answer/id #uuid "a5f7a5ec-e699-57c4-be52-69d69b469d0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698483} {:answer/id #uuid "ad1ae021-36da-5c34-9556-d90e25334ad5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698484} {:answer/id #uuid "b1ee9d33-cb51-53a3-92e1-9dd6784a62ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698485} {:answer/id #uuid "e0e74f5d-8741-552d-8c64-7dabafacd907" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm\\sqrt6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698490}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5f7a5ec-e699-57c4-be52-69d69b469d0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698483} :answer-field/id #uuid "49706acc-c0e0-518b-8261-81bd55408db2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698480}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f5e4ee0b-46a0-53fd-888f-500e5c8d2e77" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf a=\\langle x,1,0\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf b=\\langle 0,0,1\\rangle$. Given that $|\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b|=\\sqrt{5}$, find all real values of $x$.\n\nUse the determinant setup\n\n$$\n\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k\\\\x&1&0\\\\0&0&1\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nRecall that the magnitude of $\\langle u,v,w\\rangle$ is $\\sqrt{u^2+v^2+w^2}$." :question/worked-solution "Expanding the determinant along its first row gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b&=(1\\cdot1-0\\cdot0)\\mathbf i\\\\\n&\\quad-(x\\cdot1-0\\cdot0)\\mathbf j\\\\\n&\\quad+(x\\cdot0-1\\cdot0)\\mathbf k\\\\\n&=\\langle1,-x,0\\rangle.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the given magnitude to form an equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sqrt{1^2+(-x)^2+0^2}&=\\sqrt5\\\\\n1+x^2&=5\\\\\nx^2&=4\\\\\nx&=\\pm2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBoth signs are needed: when $x=2$ or $x=-2$, the magnitude is $\\sqrt{1+4}=\\sqrt5$. Therefore all real solutions are $x=-2$ and $x=2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698669 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6111f0a6-3c0e-5878-84d0-5cd97d650a3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2i-j+3k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698678} {:answer/id #uuid "a14510eb-7920-555f-87ca-ce8d0be92b35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2i+17j-3k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698685} {:answer/id #uuid "a4b7219e-479c-5590-bf60-86db83229491" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-i+3j-2k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698686} {:answer/id #uuid "b8ae8561-57c2-5808-8938-291e8d480f35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9j+3k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698689} {:answer/id #uuid "e85ee997-ecd3-5cc7-9027-4e2deecfc516" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2i+j-3k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698695}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6111f0a6-3c0e-5878-84d0-5cd97d650a3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2i-j+3k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698678} :answer-field/id #uuid "0aef6169-af73-5bdb-9a76-1eff162fbdf9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698668}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "13f57dae-66c5-5183-a9d2-c195aa95038f" :question/problem "Let $a=-4i-j-3k$ and $b=3i+2k$. Use a determinant to find $a\\times b$." :question/worked-solution "Read the coefficients in $i,j,k$ order: $a=\\langle -4,-1,-3\\rangle$ and $b=\\langle 3,0,2\\rangle$. Place $a$ above $b$ and expand along the top row with signs $+,-,+$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na\\times b&=\\begin{vmatrix}i&j&k\\\\-4&-1&-3\\\\3&0&2\\end{vmatrix}\\\\&=\\begin{vmatrix}-1&-3\\\\0&2\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}-4&-3\\\\3&2\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}-4&-1\\\\3&0\\end{vmatrix}k\\\\&=((-1)(2)-(-3)(0))i\\\\&\\quad-((-4)(2)-(-3)(3))j\\\\&\\quad+((-4)(0)-(-1)(3))k\\\\&=((-2)-(0))i\\\\&\\quad-((-8)-(-9))j\\\\&\\quad+((0)-(-3))k\\\\&=-2i-j+3k\\\\&=\\langle -2,-1,3\\rangle\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698671 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "038a232b-a8ea-5631-b8b8-21487ee21fd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4i+6j-2k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698666} {:answer/id #uuid "77ebfc21-5e78-57ad-998f-15eb37d3ee80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4i-2j-2k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698682} {:answer/id #uuid "bc49b6f2-6356-5112-a2ae-215b6f31692e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2i-2j-4k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698691} {:answer/id #uuid "e7b157e5-e3c0-5a9b-b4fb-85f0cfaf815c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4i+2j-2k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698694} {:answer/id #uuid "fdaf9e85-0661-5bf0-aed0-d1a1844bd42e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4i-4j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698699}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77ebfc21-5e78-57ad-998f-15eb37d3ee80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4i-2j-2k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698682} :answer-field/id #uuid "02de3ec0-f309-546e-84d4-988a8668687a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698665}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "20116de0-9294-5362-8aa8-82b573fcbf7e" :question/problem "Let $a=2i-2j-2k$ and $b=i-2k$. Use a determinant to find $b\\times a$." :question/worked-solution "Read the coefficients in $i,j,k$ order: $a=\\langle 2,-2,-2\\rangle$ and $b=\\langle 1,0,-2\\rangle$. Place $b$ above $a$ and expand along the top row with signs $+,-,+$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nb\\times a&=\\begin{vmatrix}i&j&k\\\\1&0&-2\\\\2&-2&-2\\end{vmatrix}\\\\&=\\begin{vmatrix}0&-2\\\\-2&-2\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}1&-2\\\\2&-2\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}1&0\\\\2&-2\\end{vmatrix}k\\\\&=((0)(-2)-(-2)(-2))i\\\\&\\quad-((1)(-2)-(-2)(2))j\\\\&\\quad+((1)(-2)-(0)(2))k\\\\&=((0)-(4))i\\\\&\\quad-((-2)-(-4))j\\\\&\\quad+((-2)-(0))k\\\\&=-4i-2j-2k\\\\&=\\langle -4,-2,-2\\rangle\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698674 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fe306e4-9a37-5242-b70a-9a0640f67c93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 12,4,1\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698670} {:answer/id #uuid "5c2902af-9015-50d1-a263-51014cc8e0eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 11,-4,1\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698676} {:answer/id #uuid "79af4257-5e1e-5c67-8b2b-0b5cb85eec60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 4,1,11\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698683} {:answer/id #uuid "ea4dd664-b528-548a-9bce-baf94944f2bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 0,3,4\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698696} {:answer/id #uuid "f9a44581-062d-587b-9c9f-039522769312" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 11,4,1\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698698}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9a44581-062d-587b-9c9f-039522769312" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\langle 11,4,1\\rangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698698} :answer-field/id #uuid "b496d2f3-a628-5d6a-b30d-215621765ddb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698688}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "474d4aff-9a8a-5edc-ae47-b9f0cd5cc32f" :question/problem "Let $a=\\langle 0,1,-4\\rangle$ and $b=\\langle -1,3,-1\\rangle$. Use a determinant to find $a\\times b$." :question/worked-solution "Read the coefficients in $i,j,k$ order: $a=\\langle 0,1,-4\\rangle$ and $b=\\langle -1,3,-1\\rangle$. Place $a$ above $b$ and expand along the top row with signs $+,-,+$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na\\times b&=\\begin{vmatrix}i&j&k\\\\0&1&-4\\\\-1&3&-1\\end{vmatrix}\\\\&=\\begin{vmatrix}1&-4\\\\3&-1\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}0&-4\\\\-1&-1\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}0&1\\\\-1&3\\end{vmatrix}k\\\\&=((1)(-1)-(-4)(3))i\\\\&\\quad-((0)(-1)-(-4)(-1))j\\\\&\\quad+((0)(3)-(1)(-1))k\\\\&=((-1)-(-12))i\\\\&\\quad-((0)-(4))j\\\\&\\quad+((0)-(-1))k\\\\&=11i+4j+k\\\\&=\\langle 11,4,1\\rangle\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698679 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04ac53ea-1b40-5efa-a717-9eebf2ea57cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6i-9j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698667} {:answer/id #uuid "28a93a50-2ca0-58c0-bce0-25a1e305b9bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698673} {:answer/id #uuid "7324a14c-b138-57eb-97f7-248a938afca5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6i+9j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698681} {:answer/id #uuid "8f1f7285-d94c-5db3-9a63-7760a0248455" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9i-6k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698684} {:answer/id #uuid "a8bd9b53-ae66-52e9-bd48-d3eb6ecc6130" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0i+0j+0k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698687}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7324a14c-b138-57eb-97f7-248a938afca5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6i+9j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698681} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb77bb28-3dba-5858-9cc4-15fe28bc0849" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698690}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "69f53331-cd90-5590-a002-0bec5637d1d8" :question/problem "Let $a=3i+2j-3k$ and $b=3k$. Use a determinant to find $b\\times a$." :question/worked-solution "Read the coefficients in $i,j,k$ order: $a=\\langle 3,2,-3\\rangle$ and $b=\\langle 0,0,3\\rangle$. Place $b$ above $a$ and expand along the top row with signs $+,-,+$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nb\\times a&=\\begin{vmatrix}i&j&k\\\\0&0&3\\\\3&2&-3\\end{vmatrix}\\\\&=\\begin{vmatrix}0&3\\\\2&-3\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}0&3\\\\3&-3\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}0&0\\\\3&2\\end{vmatrix}k\\\\&=((0)(-3)-(3)(2))i\\\\&\\quad-((0)(-3)-(3)(3))j\\\\&\\quad+((0)(2)-(0)(3))k\\\\&=((0)-(6))i\\\\&\\quad-((0)-(9))j\\\\&\\quad+((0)-(0))k\\\\&=-6i+9j\\\\&=\\langle -6,9,0\\rangle\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698692 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48d0e76d-fbeb-5f76-a272-7848d08f39a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12j+16k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698675} {:answer/id #uuid "5fb16915-c0aa-56e0-82cc-c4aa8fd7ae45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698677} {:answer/id #uuid "72237760-eacf-5ebf-b124-4c62173c5c6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698680} {:answer/id #uuid "e2953e39-91c8-5b0c-944d-654b02af9092" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698693} {:answer/id #uuid "f36acb72-55ee-57d1-be34-6fa03b184246" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16i-12k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698697}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f36acb72-55ee-57d1-be34-6fa03b184246" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16i-12k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698697} :answer-field/id #uuid "244fd8c5-7690-5ab9-bd54-2c5c9cc6b281" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698672}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d13f8592-1da3-59f8-9729-1e21910388da" :question/problem "Let $a=3i+4j+4k$ and $b=4j$. Use a determinant to find $b\\times a$." :question/worked-solution "Read the coefficients in $i,j,k$ order: $a=\\langle 3,4,4\\rangle$ and $b=\\langle 0,4,0\\rangle$. Place $b$ above $a$ and expand along the top row with signs $+,-,+$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nb\\times a&=\\begin{vmatrix}i&j&k\\\\0&4&0\\\\3&4&4\\end{vmatrix}\\\\&=\\begin{vmatrix}4&0\\\\4&4\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}0&0\\\\3&4\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}0&4\\\\3&4\\end{vmatrix}k\\\\&=((4)(4)-(0)(4))i\\\\&\\quad-((0)(4)-(0)(3))j\\\\&\\quad+((0)(4)-(4)(3))k\\\\&=((16)-(0))i\\\\&\\quad-((0)-(0))j\\\\&\\quad+((0)-(12))k\\\\&=16i-12k\\\\&=\\langle 16,0,-12\\rangle\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698852 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9cb979a1-4974-5260-b76c-c6740ee1d409" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698858}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9cb979a1-4974-5260-b76c-c6740ee1d409" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698858} :answer-field/id #uuid "082594b6-fee5-5e5e-888f-c43d0793c35e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698850} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9a395f0-d6cf-5dda-87a0-bb9ae5aa7ae6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698865}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9a395f0-d6cf-5dda-87a0-bb9ae5aa7ae6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698865} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d349010-a459-58a8-ad0f-cf03fa083a64" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698851}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "138d914d-ce26-57f0-89f4-c7d84a94c12f" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf a=\\langle -3,-2,x\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf b=\\langle -3,2,0\\rangle$. Given that $|\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b|=\\sqrt{157}$, find all real values of $x$.\n\nIn **ascending order**, the values are $x=$ {{field-1}} and $x=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, compute each signed component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b&=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k\\\\-3&-2&x\\\\-3&2&0\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\nc_1&=\\begin{vmatrix}-2&x\\\\2&0\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\n&=((-2)(0)-(x)(2))=- 2x\\\\\nc_2&=-\\begin{vmatrix}-3&x\\\\-3&0\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\n&=-((-3)(0)-(x)(-3))=- 3x\\\\\nc_3&=\\begin{vmatrix}-3&-2\\\\-3&2\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\n&=((-3)(2)-(-2)(-3))=-12\\\\\n\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b&=\\langle - 2x,- 3x,-12\\rangle\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $N(x)$ be the sum of the squared components. Compute the magnitude, square both sides, and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nN(x)&=(- 2x)^2\\\\\n&\\quad +(- 3x)^2\\\\\n&\\quad +(-12)^2\\\\\n&=13x^{2} + 144\\\\\n|\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b|&=\\sqrt{13x^{2} + 144}\\\\\n\\sqrt{13x^{2} + 144}&=\\sqrt{157}\\\\\n13x^{2} + 144&=157\\\\\n13x^2&=13\\\\\nx^2&=1\\\\\nx&=\\pm\\sqrt{1}\\\\\nx&=-1\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x=1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCheck each candidate in the squared magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nN(-1)&=157=157\\\\\nN(1)&=157=157\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere $N(x)$ is the sum of the squared cross-product components. Both magnitudes are nonnegative, so these checks also verify the original magnitude equation. In ascending order, all real solutions are $x=-1$ and $x=1$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698857 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b75574fe-4bef-52d4-b2a7-33757ac2ccd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698862}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b75574fe-4bef-52d4-b2a7-33757ac2ccd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698862} :answer-field/id #uuid "037f632a-f7d8-5a05-a252-edf5017b4a9a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698848} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3fd96e15-cdd0-5c5c-8bfc-26b603bc5b9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698855}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3fd96e15-cdd0-5c5c-8bfc-26b603bc5b9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698855} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f834628-eae0-56da-8ac0-6d4d4359c89d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698859}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7a192f65-82bf-5149-867a-6b037650bb4b" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf a=\\langle -1,2x,-2\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf b=\\langle 1,0,1\\rangle$. Given that $|\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b|=\\frac{\\sqrt{41}}{3}$, find all real values of $x$.\n\nIn **ascending order**, the values are $x=$ {{field-1}} and $x=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, compute each signed component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b&=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k\\\\-1&2x&-2\\\\1&0&1\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\nc_1&=\\begin{vmatrix}2x&-2\\\\0&1\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\n&=((2x)(1)-(-2)(0))=2x\\\\\nc_2&=-\\begin{vmatrix}-1&-2\\\\1&1\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\n&=-((-1)(1)-(-2)(1))=-1\\\\\nc_3&=\\begin{vmatrix}-1&2x\\\\1&0\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\n&=((-1)(0)-(2x)(1))=- 2x\\\\\n\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b&=\\langle 2x,-1,- 2x\\rangle\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $N(x)$ be the sum of the squared components. Compute the magnitude, square both sides, and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nN(x)&=(2x)^2\\\\\n&\\quad +(-1)^2\\\\\n&\\quad +(- 2x)^2\\\\\n&=8x^{2} + 1\\\\\n|\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b|&=\\sqrt{8x^{2} + 1}\\\\\n\\sqrt{8x^{2} + 1}&=\\frac{\\sqrt{41}}{3}\\\\\n8x^{2} + 1&=\\frac{41}{9}\\\\\n8x^2&=\\frac{32}{9}\\\\\nx^2&=\\frac{4}{9}\\\\\nx&=\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac{4}{9}}\\\\\nx&=- \\frac{2}{3}\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x=\\frac{2}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCheck each candidate in the squared magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nN\\left(- \\frac{2}{3}\\right)&=\\frac{41}{9}=\\frac{41}{9}\\\\\nN\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)&=\\frac{41}{9}=\\frac{41}{9}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere $N(x)$ is the sum of the squared cross-product components. Both magnitudes are nonnegative, so these checks also verify the original magnitude equation. In ascending order, all real solutions are $x=- \\frac{2}{3}$ and $x=\\frac{2}{3}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698861 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d84cbd7-c8dd-56d9-ac0a-2a248daa2b18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698853}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d84cbd7-c8dd-56d9-ac0a-2a248daa2b18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698853} :answer-field/id #uuid "4301e71e-c7ba-5527-9617-ed912b27aae4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698856} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa070f5f-94e8-5c07-9bb8-683af58c650b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa070f5f-94e8-5c07-9bb8-683af58c650b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698871} :answer-field/id #uuid "caa1769e-181e-519a-bcba-1bda70279857" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698866}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b3fcb99b-6ece-52d6-9a11-1a566a308b97" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf a=\\langle - 2x,2,-2\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf b=\\langle x,3,-1\\rangle$. Given that $|\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b|=4 \\sqrt{6}$, find all real values of $x$.\n\nIn **ascending order**, the values are $x=$ {{field-1}} and $x=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, compute each signed component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b&=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k\\\\- 2x&2&-2\\\\x&3&-1\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\nc_1&=\\begin{vmatrix}2&-2\\\\3&-1\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\n&=((2)(-1)-(-2)(3))=4\\\\\nc_2&=-\\begin{vmatrix}- 2x&-2\\\\x&-1\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\n&=-((- 2x)(-1)-(-2)(x))=- 4x\\\\\nc_3&=\\begin{vmatrix}- 2x&2\\\\x&3\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\n&=((- 2x)(3)-(2)(x))=- 8x\\\\\n\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b&=\\langle 4,- 4x,- 8x\\rangle\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $N(x)$ be the sum of the squared components. Compute the magnitude, square both sides, and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nN(x)&=(4)^2\\\\\n&\\quad +(- 4x)^2\\\\\n&\\quad +(- 8x)^2\\\\\n&=80x^{2} + 16\\\\\n|\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b|&=\\sqrt{80x^{2} + 16}\\\\\n\\sqrt{80x^{2} + 16}&=4 \\sqrt{6}\\\\\n80x^{2} + 16&=96\\\\\n80x^2&=80\\\\\nx^2&=1\\\\\nx&=\\pm\\sqrt{1}\\\\\nx&=-1\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x=1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCheck each candidate in the squared magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nN(-1)&=96=96\\\\\nN(1)&=96=96\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere $N(x)$ is the sum of the squared cross-product components. Both magnitudes are nonnegative, so these checks also verify the original magnitude equation. In ascending order, all real solutions are $x=-1$ and $x=1$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698863 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05ec99aa-f4c0-52ee-859a-9238db088e97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698849}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05ec99aa-f4c0-52ee-859a-9238db088e97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698849} :answer-field/id #uuid "01a60d16-ad8a-5147-acce-c03697caa992" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698847} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0fb7741-76ca-5bf0-b7b1-601071012e40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698870}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0fb7741-76ca-5bf0-b7b1-601071012e40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698870} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa7a0785-95e8-50f1-be34-bfbd874a51c1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698860}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bdf895fb-3f98-5d02-9ad5-3498f1fc1cdc" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf a=\\langle -3,0,-2\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf b=\\langle 1,x,0\\rangle$. Given that $|\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b|=2 \\sqrt{14}$, find all real values of $x$.\n\nIn **ascending order**, the values are $x=$ {{field-1}} and $x=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, compute each signed component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b&=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k\\\\-3&0&-2\\\\1&x&0\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\nc_1&=\\begin{vmatrix}0&-2\\\\x&0\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\n&=((0)(0)-(-2)(x))=2x\\\\\nc_2&=-\\begin{vmatrix}-3&-2\\\\1&0\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\n&=-((-3)(0)-(-2)(1))=-2\\\\\nc_3&=\\begin{vmatrix}-3&0\\\\1&x\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\n&=((-3)(x)-(0)(1))=- 3x\\\\\n\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b&=\\langle 2x,-2,- 3x\\rangle\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $N(x)$ be the sum of the squared components. Compute the magnitude, square both sides, and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nN(x)&=(2x)^2\\\\\n&\\quad +(-2)^2\\\\\n&\\quad +(- 3x)^2\\\\\n&=13x^{2} + 4\\\\\n|\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b|&=\\sqrt{13x^{2} + 4}\\\\\n\\sqrt{13x^{2} + 4}&=2 \\sqrt{14}\\\\\n13x^{2} + 4&=56\\\\\n13x^2&=52\\\\\nx^2&=4\\\\\nx&=\\pm\\sqrt{4}\\\\\nx&=-2\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x=2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCheck each candidate in the squared magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nN(-2)&=56=56\\\\\nN(2)&=56=56\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere $N(x)$ is the sum of the squared cross-product components. Both magnitudes are nonnegative, so these checks also verify the original magnitude equation. In ascending order, all real solutions are $x=-2$ and $x=2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698868 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cdb57b68-c048-5a62-a575-7036650f7cc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698867}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdb57b68-c048-5a62-a575-7036650f7cc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698867} :answer-field/id #uuid "375bdd5a-edcd-5667-b631-90384619d7c5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698854} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c174d646-ecb0-5e7e-af9f-bc15d4fb94b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698864}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c174d646-ecb0-5e7e-af9f-bc15d4fb94b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698864} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1d7fe8c-0df1-5389-a80b-558f2352f62a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698869}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d087877b-2d60-51fd-9365-72144f022826" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf a=\\langle -1,-3,x\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf b=\\langle 1,2,2x\\rangle$. Given that $|\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b|=\\sqrt{366}$, find all real values of $x$.\n\nIn **ascending order**, the values are $x=$ {{field-1}} and $x=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, compute each signed component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b&=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k\\\\-1&-3&x\\\\1&2&2x\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\nc_1&=\\begin{vmatrix}-3&x\\\\2&2x\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\n&=((-3)(2x)-(x)(2))=- 8x\\\\\nc_2&=-\\begin{vmatrix}-1&x\\\\1&2x\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\n&=-((-1)(2x)-(x)(1))=3x\\\\\nc_3&=\\begin{vmatrix}-1&-3\\\\1&2\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\n&=((-1)(2)-(-3)(1))=1\\\\\n\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b&=\\langle - 8x,3x,1\\rangle\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $N(x)$ be the sum of the squared components. Compute the magnitude, square both sides, and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nN(x)&=(- 8x)^2\\\\\n&\\quad +(3x)^2\\\\\n&\\quad +(1)^2\\\\\n&=73x^{2} + 1\\\\\n|\\mathbf a\\times\\mathbf b|&=\\sqrt{73x^{2} + 1}\\\\\n\\sqrt{73x^{2} + 1}&=\\sqrt{366}\\\\\n73x^{2} + 1&=366\\\\\n73x^2&=365\\\\\nx^2&=5\\\\\nx&=\\pm\\sqrt{5}\\\\\nx&=- \\sqrt{5}\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x=\\sqrt{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCheck each candidate in the squared magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nN(- \\sqrt{5})&=366=366\\\\\nN(\\sqrt{5})&=366=366\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere $N(x)$ is the sum of the squared cross-product components. Both magnitudes are nonnegative, so these checks also verify the original magnitude equation. In ascending order, all real solutions are $x=- \\sqrt{5}$ and $x=\\sqrt{5}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699606 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41049cde-be3e-5f34-b27f-8051cf06551d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\,\\mathbf i-2\\,\\mathbf j+2\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699612} {:answer/id #uuid "b69d3265-0b74-5cae-943e-8d5b02f7f9a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,\\mathbf i+2\\,\\mathbf j-2\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699619} {:answer/id #uuid "b84ae09c-d4ec-51dd-9c65-fb618277e450" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7\\,\\mathbf i+2\\,\\mathbf j+2\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699620} {:answer/id #uuid "c284a812-e9fe-536c-8367-753d676e2a36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7\\,\\mathbf i-2\\,\\mathbf j+6\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699622} {:answer/id #uuid "d0da9a7c-89b1-5463-b24b-fe94b59e7cf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7\\,\\mathbf i-2\\,\\mathbf j+2\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699623}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0da9a7c-89b1-5463-b24b-fe94b59e7cf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7\\,\\mathbf i-2\\,\\mathbf j+2\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699623} :answer-field/id #uuid "86a7916f-c22d-5122-8a59-fd0b5fd654ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699616}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "026f4d1e-da9e-51a1-93f7-646ae070dc9d" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf F=(xy^2+yz)\\,\\mathbf i+(x^2y+xz^2)\\,\\mathbf j+(xy+y^2z+xz)\\,\\mathbf k$. Evaluate $\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F$ at $(1,-1,2)$." :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j+R\\,\\mathbf k$. The determinant expansion keeps the middle cofactor negative:\n\n$$\n\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i & \\mathbf j & \\mathbf k \\\\ \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial z} \\\\ xy^2+yz & x^2y+xz^2 & xy+y^2z+xz\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate before substituting any coordinates, treating the other variables as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F &=(R_y-Q_z)\\,\\mathbf i-(R_x-P_z)\\,\\mathbf j+(Q_x-P_y)\\,\\mathbf k \\\\ &=\\bigl((x+2yz)-2xz\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf i-\\bigl((y+z)-y\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf j \\\\ &\\quad+\\bigl((2xy+z^2)-(2xy+z)\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf k \\\\ &=(x+2yz-2xz)\\,\\mathbf i-z\\,\\mathbf j+(z^2-z)\\,\\mathbf k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $y$ terms cancel in the middle component, and the $2xy$ terms cancel in the last component. Only after taking these derivatives do we substitute the point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F)(1,-1,2)&=\\bigl(1+2(-1)(2)-2(1)(2)\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf i \\\\ &\\quad-2\\,\\mathbf j+(2^2-2)\\,\\mathbf k \\\\ &=-7\\,\\mathbf i-2\\,\\mathbf j+2\\,\\mathbf k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699610 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18298077-ac03-54fd-adf0-7b850ad8f298" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2z\\,\\mathbf j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699607} {:answer/id #uuid "1fda3936-b054-5ed5-9428-72c60957bb37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\mathbf i+(2z-1)\\,\\mathbf j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699608} {:answer/id #uuid "3ebff7bc-3fc8-5363-811f-6ed05f2ffdfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2z+1)\\,\\mathbf j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699611} {:answer/id #uuid "4f4d08af-b995-5789-969a-dd899c29cc63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1-2z)\\,\\mathbf j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699613} {:answer/id #uuid "b0c98eaf-a33c-5604-983a-3b5551981338" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2z-1)\\,\\mathbf j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699617}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0c98eaf-a33c-5604-983a-3b5551981338" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2z-1)\\,\\mathbf j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699617} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc125385-a4b0-5bc6-8aca-aabdd9ea8f7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699626}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3c635ddb-68ed-585f-9c7b-1d504525a10e" :question/problem "Given that $\\mathbf F(x,y,z)=z^2\\,\\mathbf i+3y\\,\\mathbf j+x\\,\\mathbf k$, what is $\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F$?" :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j+R\\,\\mathbf k$. The determinant expansion keeps the middle cofactor negative:\n\n$$\n\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i & \\mathbf j & \\mathbf k \\\\ \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial z} \\\\ z^2 & 3y & x\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate before substituting any coordinates, treating the other variables as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F &=(R_y-Q_z)\\,\\mathbf i-(R_x-P_z)\\,\\mathbf j+(Q_x-P_y)\\,\\mathbf k \\\\ &=(0-0)\\,\\mathbf i-(1-2z)\\,\\mathbf j+(0-0)\\,\\mathbf k \\\\ &=(2z-1)\\,\\mathbf j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the curl is $(2z-1)\\,\\mathbf j$. In particular, differentiating $3y$ with respect to $z$ or $x$ gives zero."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699615 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33f54ae4-f02c-5b08-b0d9-6d033caec146" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\mathbf i-3\\,\\mathbf j+6\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699609} {:answer/id #uuid "b26e1ec9-db48-5307-98de-34476e3def3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\mathbf i+2\\,\\mathbf j+2\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699618} {:answer/id #uuid "bc76c50c-71fb-5a4c-9f90-f75a43abc276" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\mathbf i-2\\,\\mathbf j+2\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699621} {:answer/id #uuid "e7f4c6a6-2bef-5df8-8d24-3091004e229d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\mathbf i-2\\,\\mathbf j-2\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699624} {:answer/id #uuid "e8091a91-1e18-544d-a2f5-76e61e14be02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\mathbf i+2\\,\\mathbf j-2\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699625}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7f4c6a6-2bef-5df8-8d24-3091004e229d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\mathbf i-2\\,\\mathbf j-2\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699624} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f7b14f5-2992-5442-99d9-fcd4bbe85496" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699614}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "66e15933-2642-5ab1-a745-617af7c54247" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf F=(xy+z)\\,\\mathbf i+yz\\,\\mathbf j+xz\\,\\mathbf k$. Evaluate $\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F$ at $(2,-1,3)$." :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j+R\\,\\mathbf k$. The determinant expansion keeps the middle cofactor negative:\n\n$$\n\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i & \\mathbf j & \\mathbf k \\\\ \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial z} \\\\ xy+z & yz & xz\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate before substituting any coordinates, treating the other variables as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F &=(R_y-Q_z)\\,\\mathbf i-(R_x-P_z)\\,\\mathbf j+(Q_x-P_y)\\,\\mathbf k \\\\ &=(0-y)\\,\\mathbf i-(z-1)\\,\\mathbf j+(0-x)\\,\\mathbf k \\\\ &=-y\\,\\mathbf i+(1-z)\\,\\mathbf j-x\\,\\mathbf k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow evaluate the curl, rather than the original field:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F)(2,-1,3)&=-(-1)\\,\\mathbf i+(1-3)\\,\\mathbf j-2\\,\\mathbf k \\\\ &=\\mathbf i-2\\,\\mathbf j-2\\,\\mathbf k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699686 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0393252c-de9f-50a7-b576-585c0e784d45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699679} {:answer/id #uuid "0b88530c-3f7c-5b71-806b-824cbf32bb3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699680}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0393252c-de9f-50a7-b576-585c0e784d45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699679} :answer-field/id #uuid "25563af6-679a-55a4-af92-10778ef8c366" :answer-field/key "$\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F\\ne\\mathbf 0$ everywhere" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699683} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4cf8ec9f-2c05-50cb-b2ae-8e07792b1e99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699695} {:answer/id #uuid "ee6a1608-20b1-5dc8-9dc3-5e78f33852ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699714}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4cf8ec9f-2c05-50cb-b2ae-8e07792b1e99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699695} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b07ac59-13fb-5311-82c5-816e7b4c4d1a" :answer-field/key "$\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F$ points in the negative $z$-direction everywhere" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699685} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "430f48d2-02da-5e88-8997-6a913b4488c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699693} {:answer/id #uuid "e2b042c3-938b-5928-ab5a-f19fde69557c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "430f48d2-02da-5e88-8997-6a913b4488c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699693} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a8bae54-3157-54ac-b37e-da4f218e42b1" :answer-field/key "$\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F=\\mathbf 0$ everywhere" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699699} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cb28fd6-35ae-53d8-bb09-1a64a70e86b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699700} {:answer/id #uuid "7aadf364-cf07-54a7-8803-d2995eaadb47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699705}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7aadf364-cf07-54a7-8803-d2995eaadb47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699705} :answer-field/id #uuid "76b8d089-b7fe-5dd5-ba01-fd574cb357e3" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf F$ is not irrotational" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699703}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2b8a97dd-b58c-57ac-b51f-51bdc97cadaf" :question/problem "![Vector field with arrows drawn to a common scale.](images/0b/0bd8cbd4a845ad62c4d1834a9b6d12675846291b9a1a88b37ad9933151cb75b8.png)\n\nThe diagram shows a vector field $\\mathbf F$ on $\\mathbb R^3$. Its $z$-component is zero, and it is independent of $z$. View the $xy$-plane from the positive $z$-axis, so positive $z$ points out of the page.\n\nBoth components vary linearly throughout the domain. The horizontal component increases with $y$ at exactly the same rate that the vertical component increases with $x$. The horizontal component does not change with $x$, and the vertical component does not change with $y$.\n\nWhich statements are true everywhere? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Consider both components of the flow around a small paddlewheel with its axle parallel to the $z$-axis.\n\n- The horizontal flow is more rightward above the center than below it. This contributes a **clockwise** turn.\n- The vertical flow is more upward to the right of the center than to the left. This contributes a **counterclockwise** turn.\n\n![The two component fields produce opposite rotational effects.](images/f9/f9eacfb22ef653c9edc981a0c1ce62c6d35fe2d8015b99177e4a68c599912e66.png)\n\nThe stated rates are equal, so these opposite rotational effects cancel exactly. This cancellation occurs around every point, because the rates are constant throughout the domain. The wheel does not spin, even though the arrows vary in direction and length.\n\nTherefore $\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F=\\mathbf 0$ everywhere, and $\\mathbf F$ is irrotational. Zero curl has no direction.\n\nSelect only “$\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F=\\mathbf 0$ everywhere.” The nonzero-curl statement, the negative $z$-direction statement, and “$\\mathbf F$ is not irrotational” are all false."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699701 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71cc1e58-5abe-517b-8c26-9e1a8728db2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699702} {:answer/id #uuid "ca76601e-488c-5ca4-87ed-36b885cef78f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699711}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca76601e-488c-5ca4-87ed-36b885cef78f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699711} :answer-field/id #uuid "35178f80-3459-5884-ada2-03a0227652ed" :answer-field/key "$\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F=\\mathbf 0$ everywhere" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699689} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a162553-02bf-5e54-be96-a40ef432a51a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699704} {:answer/id #uuid "83f3b1ea-fe4e-56c3-9d94-66b267b53356" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699706}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83f3b1ea-fe4e-56c3-9d94-66b267b53356" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699706} :answer-field/id #uuid "40330d54-8da7-5933-9b94-306abe99754b" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf F$ is irrotational" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699690} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30aec6d2-5e5c-5bb2-97b7-c5a797ee1925" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699687} {:answer/id #uuid "31215440-7e69-5158-b6ac-4ab1b2c98aa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699688}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31215440-7e69-5158-b6ac-4ab1b2c98aa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699688} :answer-field/id #uuid "56ba1e5b-c755-5634-8beb-7aaf55f98dca" :answer-field/key "$\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F\\ne\\mathbf 0$ everywhere" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699697} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b392fc3-17b3-5273-a286-3248f4dac7fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699694} {:answer/id #uuid "5477bfa2-2785-5476-9367-6fd7111b98f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699696}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b392fc3-17b3-5273-a286-3248f4dac7fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699694} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fd1ef4b-487e-5293-aaf8-cca1f56ce616" :answer-field/key "$\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F$ points in the positive $z$-direction everywhere" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699709}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5ddfb17d-b307-59f5-9de7-a7750b88f79f" :question/problem "![Vector field with arrows drawn to a common scale.](images/2a/2af371cb122ed5519856947c3784d64f5f93dc70189b05b7e364ce616d837153.png)\n\nThe diagram shows a vector field $\\mathbf F$ on $\\mathbb R^3$. Its $z$-component is zero, and it is independent of $z$. View the $xy$-plane from the positive $z$-axis, so positive $z$ points out of the page.\n\nEvery arrow has the same direction and length, and this uniform pattern continues throughout the domain.\n\nWhich statements are true everywhere? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Imagine a small paddlewheel with its axle parallel to the $z$-axis. The arrows at its upper and lower sides are identical, as are the arrows at its left and right sides. The flow can carry the wheel along, but does not make it spin.\n\nThe comparison below distinguishes unequal sideways pushes (left) from equal sideways pushes (right). The present field has equal pushes, like the right panel.\n\n![](images/59/594106633e422d24b9fea113d24fb6367fdef5ac52724931860e4163e33ce992.png)\n\nThus $\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F=\\mathbf 0$ everywhere. A field with zero curl everywhere is **irrotational**. A zero vector has no direction, so it cannot point in the positive $z$-direction.\n\nSelect “$\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F=\\mathbf 0$ everywhere” and “$\\mathbf F$ is irrotational.” Leave the other two statements unselected."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699715 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "239580c9-1c71-5a96-8ca0-e277a21504da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699681} {:answer/id #uuid "f6943817-9a82-5830-bdb7-9070767009a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699716}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6943817-9a82-5830-bdb7-9070767009a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699716} :answer-field/id #uuid "28e2b21e-ce53-5443-b6c4-1d346eed7234" :answer-field/key "$\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F$ points in the negative $z$-direction everywhere" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699684} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42b05463-f79c-53e7-a983-d35aa7a511c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699692} {:answer/id #uuid "f83201a1-43ac-5597-8af3-9f2c63588ef4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699717}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f83201a1-43ac-5597-8af3-9f2c63588ef4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699717} :answer-field/id #uuid "58227350-16f3-5dca-a6ca-2f3d5ebab0ec" :answer-field/key "$\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F=\\mathbf 0$ everywhere" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699698} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2491ba4a-0442-53e3-bbc3-3cfc86aa81c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699682} {:answer/id #uuid "da13ba80-3ab1-576d-9409-d68b9bad47e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699712}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2491ba4a-0442-53e3-bbc3-3cfc86aa81c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699682} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ccddf86-1c3b-5e7f-9a0d-508589b28afe" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf F$ is irrotational" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699708} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40fa0b91-0968-5d08-93f6-be2e9c42ea6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699691} {:answer/id #uuid "8927ab0e-64c6-5bd1-8ea1-4c9056c4cdf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699707}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8927ab0e-64c6-5bd1-8ea1-4c9056c4cdf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699707} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8ec9fed-102d-59e2-8e85-625eb95650bf" :answer-field/key "$\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F\\ne\\mathbf 0$ everywhere" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699710}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f4482864-4aef-507a-9192-6d1ecb7048dd" :question/problem "![Vector field with arrows drawn to a common scale.](images/7a/7a955f42458ed8a43ae5748a1e7ee442d328df5ca3e8b85918c31b9dc2ba2a36.png)\n\nThe diagram shows a vector field $\\mathbf F$ on $\\mathbb R^3$. Its $z$-component is zero, and it is independent of $z$. View the $xy$-plane from the positive $z$-axis, so positive $z$ points out of the page.\n\nAll vectors are horizontal. Their horizontal component increases at a constant rate as $y$ increases and does not change with $x$; this pattern continues throughout the domain.\n\nWhich statements are true everywhere? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Imagine a small paddlewheel with its axle parallel to the $z$-axis. Just above its center the horizontal flow is more rightward than just below. This difference makes the wheel turn **clockwise** as viewed from positive $z$. There is no vertical flow to oppose this rotation.\n\nThe left panel below illustrates this unequal-push effect; the right panel shows equal pushes that would not cause rotation.\n\n![](images/59/594106633e422d24b9fea113d24fb6367fdef5ac52724931860e4163e33ce992.png)\n\nThe constant difference in horizontal flow occurs around every point, so the curl is nonzero everywhere. Wrap your right-hand fingers clockwise: your thumb points into the page, in the **negative $z$-direction**. Since the curl is nonzero, the field is not irrotational.\n\nSelect “$\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F\\ne\\mathbf 0$ everywhere” and “$\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F$ points in the negative $z$-direction everywhere.” Leave the other two statements unselected."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699816 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "This gives only $Q_x$; also subtract $P_y=x$." :answer/id #uuid "0ac668ea-4b3c-5562-9e7f-21dfc96b2edf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699811} {:answer/feedback "This is $Q_y-P_x$. Scalar curl uses $Q_x-P_y$." :answer/id #uuid "0fe64014-cf0d-5d8a-ad80-8ccb00837838" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^2+3y^2-2x-y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699812} {:answer/feedback "Subtract $P_y=x$ from $Q_x=2xy$." :answer/id #uuid "63f52878-4dd9-5d26-a551-54d832deebb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy+x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699818} {:answer/feedback "Correct: $Q_x=2xy$ and $P_y=x$." :answer/id #uuid "7521e81c-88aa-56ff-9341-8548fd3c0ec0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699820} {:answer/feedback "This reverses the subtraction. Scalar curl is $Q_x-P_y$." :answer/id #uuid "e1c9fcde-81e9-5b44-baca-809e588ac33a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-2xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699830}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Correct: $Q_x=2xy$ and $P_y=x$." :answer/id #uuid "7521e81c-88aa-56ff-9341-8548fd3c0ec0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699820} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ac6aa74-22ee-5ef9-bf88-a4991631ca80" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699814}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "56b52fff-0bdb-5869-97b1-d3dededc7d3c" :question/problem "Given that $\\mathbf F(x,y)=(x^2+xy)\\,\\mathbf i+(x^2y+y^3)\\,\\mathbf j$, what is the scalar curl of $\\mathbf F$?" :question/worked-solution "For $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$, the scalar curl is $Q_x-P_y$. In each partial derivative, hold the other variable constant.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}-\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}\n&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(x^2y+y^3)-\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(x^2+xy)\\\\\n&=2xy-x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe term $y^3$ is constant with respect to $x$, and $x^2$ is constant with respect to $y$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699821 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Each product derivative has two terms: $Q_x=\\ln 2+\\frac12$ and $P_y=e+e$ at $(1,1)$." :answer/id #uuid "1753f3fa-729e-5df7-8fab-cc7d01ac5b36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac12-e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699813} {:answer/feedback "Correct: subtract $P_y=2e$ from $Q_x=\\ln 2+\\frac12$." :answer/id #uuid "626f0026-6c26-5555-a6be-2549a57ee40b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln 2+\\frac12-2e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699817} {:answer/feedback "The product rule gives $Q_x=\\ln(x+y)+x/(x+y)$; retain the $\\ln 2$ term." :answer/id #uuid "7fcf61ac-bdf7-5413-84ed-8d1d9f424454" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac12-2e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699822} {:answer/feedback "The product rule gives $P_y=e^{xy}+xy e^{xy}$, which is $2e$ at $(1,1)$." :answer/id #uuid "9183291e-b945-567e-8de6-bc0031e2bd5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln 2+\\frac12-e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699825} {:answer/feedback "This is $P_y-Q_x$. Reverse the subtraction to obtain the scalar curl." :answer/id #uuid "b81b8407-bb2f-5b85-a7bc-0734df97cbfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e-\\ln 2-\\frac12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699828}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Correct: subtract $P_y=2e$ from $Q_x=\\ln 2+\\frac12$." :answer/id #uuid "626f0026-6c26-5555-a6be-2549a57ee40b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln 2+\\frac12-2e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699817} :answer-field/id #uuid "8988f4bf-e8ae-5b12-af48-30a3334aa270" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699823}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7c282bf6-76df-59aa-8ea2-5040f4209860" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y)=y e^{xy}\\,\\mathbf i+x\\ln(x+y)\\,\\mathbf j$, defined where $x+y>0$. Evaluate the scalar curl of $\\mathbf F$ at the point $(1,1)$." :question/worked-solution "For $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$, the scalar curl is $Q_x-P_y$. Both cross-partials require the product rule and the chain rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}\n&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\bigl(x\\ln(x+y)\\bigr)\\\\\n&=\\ln(x+y)+\\frac{x}{x+y},\\\\[4pt]\n\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}\n&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\bigl(y e^{xy}\\bigr)\\\\\n&=e^{xy}+xy e^{xy}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nQ_x-P_y&=\\ln(x+y)+\\frac{x}{x+y}-e^{xy}-xy e^{xy}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe point $(1,1)$ lies in the domain because $1+1>0$. Evaluating gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(Q_x-P_y)(1,1)&=\\ln 2+\\frac12-e-e\\\\\n&=\\ln 2+\\frac12-2e.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699829 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "This evaluates $Q_x$ alone; subtract $P_y=2\\pi$ as well." :answer/id #uuid "4b8e160d-5bbc-5dc5-8e05-933ec1fc8dbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699815} {:answer/feedback "The chain-rule term $Q_x=\\pi\\cos\\pi=-\\pi$ is nonzero." :answer/id #uuid "6d2ae8e6-b33e-5247-ab1c-4bbd2612547e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699819} {:answer/feedback "This reverses the subtraction. Scalar curl is $Q_x-P_y$." :answer/id #uuid "8f85560e-2136-5532-93bd-3db8171f3217" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699824} {:answer/feedback "Correct: $\\pi\\cos\\pi-2\\pi=-3\\pi$." :answer/id #uuid "933384f5-2ef5-5b31-9112-cb0657dc85ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699826} {:answer/feedback "Use $\\cos\\pi=-1$, so $\\pi\\cos\\pi-2\\pi=-3\\pi$." :answer/id #uuid "9be392f6-5646-57c6-94ae-e20b00440b91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699827}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Correct: $\\pi\\cos\\pi-2\\pi=-3\\pi$." :answer/id #uuid "933384f5-2ef5-5b31-9112-cb0657dc85ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699826} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3ad2e51-c4d1-5743-bfa1-aa8dd3b619be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699831}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bd1948fd-b1bb-5dca-885a-3160f2f10fd0" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y)=(x^2+y^2)\\,\\mathbf i+\\sin(xy)\\,\\mathbf j$. Evaluate the scalar curl of $\\mathbf F$ at the point $(1,\\pi)$." :question/worked-solution "For $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$, the scalar curl is $Q_x-P_y$. Differentiate before substituting the point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}-\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}\n&=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\sin(xy)-\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(x^2+y^2)\\\\\n&=y\\cos(xy)-2y.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe factor $y$ in the first term comes from the chain rule. At $(1,\\pi)$,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(Q_x-P_y)(1,\\pi)&=\\pi\\cos(\\pi)-2\\pi\\\\\n&=-\\pi-2\\pi\\\\\n&=-3\\pi.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699941 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04585f0b-9a1a-50af-af67-d981244b608a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\,\\mathbf i-2\\,\\mathbf j-\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699931} {:answer/id #uuid "0f9c368f-a2dc-5d9b-9cf7-f42f24152a89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\,\\mathbf i-4\\,\\mathbf j+5\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699933} {:answer/id #uuid "577bbf05-5419-531e-8f9b-73e84772457b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,\\mathbf i-4\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699939} {:answer/id #uuid "caca3ad6-bca6-5e58-9018-9d5fb735807a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\,\\mathbf i+5\\,\\mathbf j+9\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699957} {:answer/id #uuid "dba42176-bd82-5e4a-800f-b03844bd1676" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9\\,\\mathbf i+4\\,\\mathbf j-5\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699959}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04585f0b-9a1a-50af-af67-d981244b608a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\,\\mathbf i-2\\,\\mathbf j-\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699931} :answer-field/id #uuid "956f547f-04c7-5b62-be91-809310a559ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699949}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5e688bbe-562b-532c-b58b-4f87b6400e08" :question/problem "Given the vector field\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y,z)=\\bigl(2 x^{2} + 1\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf i-\\bigl(x - 2 z\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf j-\\bigl(2 x z - y\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf k\n$$\n\nevaluate $\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F$ at $(2,1,-1)$." :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j+R\\,\\mathbf k$. The middle cofactor is negative:\n\n$$\n\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k \\\\ \\partial/\\partial x&\\partial/\\partial y&\\partial/\\partial z \\\\ 2 x^{2} + 1 & - x + 2 z & - 2 x z + y\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nTake the cross partial derivatives, holding the other coordinates constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R_y-Q_z&=\\bigl(1\\bigr)-\\bigl(2\\bigr) \\\\ &=-1 \\\\ P_z-R_x&=\\bigl(0\\bigr)-\\bigl(- 2 z\\bigr) \\\\ &=2 z \\\\ Q_x-P_y&=\\bigl(-1\\bigr)-\\bigl(0\\bigr) \\\\ &=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus\n\n$$\n\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F=-\\,\\mathbf i+2 z\\,\\mathbf j-\\,\\mathbf k\n$$\n\nSubstitute the point into these derivatives, not into the original field:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R_y-Q_z&=-1 \\\\ P_z-R_x&=2 (-1) \\\\ &=-2 \\\\ Q_x-P_y&=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore\n\n$$\n(\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F)(2,1,-1)=-\\,\\mathbf i-2\\,\\mathbf j-\\,\\mathbf k\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699942 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e97dae9-87c8-5823-bee7-4d368beea6c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 e\\,\\mathbf j-2 e\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699932} {:answer/id #uuid "7d576092-4782-5ec5-8b5c-9ad1dbf45705" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 e\\,\\mathbf j+2 e\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699947} {:answer/id #uuid "c47893a8-e38d-58eb-854f-26a82ceed487" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2 e\\,\\mathbf i+2 e\\,\\mathbf j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699956} {:answer/id #uuid "e3dc8abc-f54a-53d5-a8f6-4daa56284e49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4 e\\,\\mathbf i-2 e\\,\\mathbf j+2 e\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699960} {:answer/id #uuid "ea69ba5d-07f9-510e-af2d-9d32f0af42c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4 e\\,\\mathbf i+2 e\\,\\mathbf j+2 e\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699962}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea69ba5d-07f9-510e-af2d-9d32f0af42c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4 e\\,\\mathbf i+2 e\\,\\mathbf j+2 e\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699962} :answer-field/id #uuid "75136d2c-7f09-5391-9e1c-e75b5bdb4769" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699945}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6c263691-3ee1-5496-afc2-afbd7629312d" :question/problem "Given the vector field\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y,z)=2 x y e^{z}\\,\\mathbf j-2 y z e^{x}\\,\\mathbf k\n$$\n\nevaluate $\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F$ at $(1,1,1)$." :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j+R\\,\\mathbf k$. The middle cofactor is negative:\n\n$$\n\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k \\\\ \\partial/\\partial x&\\partial/\\partial y&\\partial/\\partial z \\\\ 0 & 2 x y e^{z} & - 2 y z e^{x}\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nTake the cross partial derivatives, holding the other coordinates constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R_y-Q_z&=\\bigl(- 2 z e^{x}\\bigr)-\\bigl(2 x y e^{z}\\bigr) \\\\ &=- 2 x y e^{z} - 2 z e^{x} \\\\ P_z-R_x&=\\bigl(0\\bigr)-\\bigl(- 2 y z e^{x}\\bigr) \\\\ &=2 y z e^{x} \\\\ Q_x-P_y&=\\bigl(2 y e^{z}\\bigr)-\\bigl(0\\bigr) \\\\ &=2 y e^{z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus\n\n$$\n\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F=-\\bigl(2 x y e^{z} + 2 z e^{x}\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf i+2 y z e^{x}\\,\\mathbf j+2 y e^{z}\\,\\mathbf k\n$$\n\nSubstitute the point into these derivatives, not into the original field:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R_y-Q_z&=- 2 (1) (1) e^{(1)} - 2 (1) e^{(1)} \\\\ &=- 4 e \\\\ P_z-R_x&=2 (1) (1) e^{(1)} \\\\ &=2 e \\\\ Q_x-P_y&=2 (1) e^{(1)} \\\\ &=2 e\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore\n\n$$\n(\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F)(1,1,1)=-4 e\\,\\mathbf i+2 e\\,\\mathbf j+2 e\\,\\mathbf k\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699955 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74e37b42-0511-57c1-b11f-404e220548ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\,\\mathbf j-2\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699944} {:answer/id #uuid "7c9facfa-347b-54e2-aedc-50158338c402" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8\\,\\mathbf j-4\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699946} {:answer/id #uuid "879f0481-7ca8-5e96-bf77-e54c3e19b726" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\,\\mathbf i-2\\,\\mathbf j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699948} {:answer/id #uuid "b85e7653-d5c6-5a8b-8840-5c619acbb866" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,\\mathbf j+2\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699952} {:answer/id #uuid "b9b365a9-0536-5e2d-a22d-09124135ea8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,\\mathbf i+2\\,\\mathbf j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699953}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b85e7653-d5c6-5a8b-8840-5c619acbb866" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,\\mathbf j+2\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699952} :answer-field/id #uuid "b343b867-7db4-5d49-be03-09f5548f6ae4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699951}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c4356916-cb29-5e8d-bf07-17e34976ee2e" :question/problem "Given the vector field\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y,z)=-2 y z\\,\\mathbf i+2 y^{2}\\,\\mathbf j-2 z^{2}\\,\\mathbf k\n$$\n\nevaluate $\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F$ at $(-1,-2,1)$." :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j+R\\,\\mathbf k$. The middle cofactor is negative:\n\n$$\n\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k \\\\ \\partial/\\partial x&\\partial/\\partial y&\\partial/\\partial z \\\\ - 2 y z & 2 y^{2} & - 2 z^{2}\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nTake the cross partial derivatives, holding the other coordinates constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R_y-Q_z&=\\bigl(0\\bigr)-\\bigl(0\\bigr) \\\\ &=0 \\\\ P_z-R_x&=\\bigl(- 2 y\\bigr)-\\bigl(0\\bigr) \\\\ &=- 2 y \\\\ Q_x-P_y&=\\bigl(0\\bigr)-\\bigl(- 2 z\\bigr) \\\\ &=2 z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus\n\n$$\n\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F=-2 y\\,\\mathbf j+2 z\\,\\mathbf k\n$$\n\nSubstitute the point into these derivatives, not into the original field:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R_y-Q_z&=0 \\\\ P_z-R_x&=- 2 (-2) \\\\ &=4 \\\\ Q_x-P_y&=2 (1) \\\\ &=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore\n\n$$\n(\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F)(-1,-2,1)=4\\,\\mathbf j+2\\,\\mathbf k\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699958 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2061aff3-37ca-5488-a421-0bb42db73653" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\mathbf i+2\\,\\mathbf j-\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699934} {:answer/id #uuid "20ece031-9da7-594c-ba03-b78c7f66979f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\,\\mathbf i+\\,\\mathbf j+\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699935} {:answer/id #uuid "7183752b-ebb5-589f-8260-e1e9ed93b9d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\,\\mathbf i+4\\,\\mathbf j+\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699943} {:answer/id #uuid "ad5ce0d1-7328-55eb-a8d9-82199c379263" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\,\\mathbf i-4\\,\\mathbf j+\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699950} {:answer/id #uuid "fe0dc631-a6d2-5068-bdc9-0d1d1be84b94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\,\\mathbf i-2\\,\\mathbf j+2\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699964}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2061aff3-37ca-5488-a421-0bb42db73653" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\mathbf i+2\\,\\mathbf j-\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699934} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a9b038c-6551-5a46-8198-d98c7976ef41" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699936}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d8e5658e-1119-5425-bf41-280ad5b1ff2f" :question/problem "Given the vector field\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y,z)=x y\\,\\mathbf i-\\bigl(2 x + 2 y z\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf j-x z\\,\\mathbf k\n$$\n\nevaluate $\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F$ at $(-1,1,2)$." :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j+R\\,\\mathbf k$. The middle cofactor is negative:\n\n$$\n\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k \\\\ \\partial/\\partial x&\\partial/\\partial y&\\partial/\\partial z \\\\ x y & - 2 x - 2 y z & - x z\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nTake the cross partial derivatives, holding the other coordinates constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R_y-Q_z&=\\bigl(0\\bigr)-\\bigl(- 2 y\\bigr) \\\\ &=2 y \\\\ P_z-R_x&=\\bigl(0\\bigr)-\\bigl(- z\\bigr) \\\\ &=z \\\\ Q_x-P_y&=\\bigl(-2\\bigr)-\\bigl(x\\bigr) \\\\ &=- x - 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus\n\n$$\n\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F=2 y\\,\\mathbf i+z\\,\\mathbf j-\\bigl(x + 2\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf k\n$$\n\nSubstitute the point into these derivatives, not into the original field:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R_y-Q_z&=2 (1) \\\\ &=2 \\\\ P_z-R_x&=(2) \\\\ &=2 \\\\ Q_x-P_y&=- (-1) - 2 \\\\ &=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore\n\n$$\n(\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F)(-1,1,2)=2\\,\\mathbf i+2\\,\\mathbf j-\\,\\mathbf k\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699961 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4073040d-5c37-50a1-b557-2a6c17bebb7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\,\\mathbf i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699938} {:answer/id #uuid "597676a6-1f04-5fcc-b86b-785d706bc2cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\mathbf i-2\\,\\mathbf j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699940} {:answer/id #uuid "ba41d716-de08-58eb-bd37-fe98536e6dba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\mathbf i-3\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699954} {:answer/id #uuid "ee11ead0-fc67-5dde-b26a-2fb0aab90bf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\mathbf i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699963} {:answer/id #uuid "fe80cf0f-432f-55b1-882e-012409bc1161" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\,\\mathbf i+2\\,\\mathbf j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699965}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe80cf0f-432f-55b1-882e-012409bc1161" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\,\\mathbf i+2\\,\\mathbf j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699965} :answer-field/id #uuid "312036fe-d1c8-5eaa-beae-1ae54c7e4811" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699937}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e6042ca0-c3ff-5196-8317-e81f3d9493ab" :question/problem "Given the vector field\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y,z)=\\,\\mathbf i-x y z\\,\\mathbf j-2 e^{x + y}\\,\\mathbf k\n$$\n\nevaluate $\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F$ at $(-1,1,0)$." :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j+R\\,\\mathbf k$. The middle cofactor is negative:\n\n$$\n\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k \\\\ \\partial/\\partial x&\\partial/\\partial y&\\partial/\\partial z \\\\ 1 & - x y z & - 2 e^{x + y}\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nTake the cross partial derivatives, holding the other coordinates constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R_y-Q_z&=\\bigl(- 2 e^{x + y}\\bigr)-\\bigl(- x y\\bigr) \\\\ &=x y - 2 e^{x + y} \\\\ P_z-R_x&=\\bigl(0\\bigr)-\\bigl(- 2 e^{x + y}\\bigr) \\\\ &=2 e^{x + y} \\\\ Q_x-P_y&=\\bigl(- y z\\bigr)-\\bigl(0\\bigr) \\\\ &=- y z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus\n\n$$\n\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F=\\bigl(x y - 2 e^{x + y}\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf i+2 e^{x + y}\\,\\mathbf j-y z\\,\\mathbf k\n$$\n\nSubstitute the point into these derivatives, not into the original field:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R_y-Q_z&=(-1) (1) - 2 e^{(-1) + (1)} \\\\ &=-3 \\\\ P_z-R_x&=2 e^{(-1) + (1)} \\\\ &=2 \\\\ Q_x-P_y&=- (1) (0) \\\\ &=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore\n\n$$\n(\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F)(-1,1,0)=-3\\,\\mathbf i+2\\,\\mathbf j\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700124 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c7c5618-6b51-59f9-ab84-b4ca43aba672" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700117} {:answer/id #uuid "ed48da7b-cff5-508e-88f3-eccebade5a08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700170}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed48da7b-cff5-508e-88f3-eccebade5a08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700170} :answer-field/id #uuid "6992c174-2316-59ff-8f02-4a22e1293035" :answer-field/key "$\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F=\\mathbf 0$ everywhere" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700137} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9eca2ad-40bf-5527-8f7b-6d281edbce1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700161} {:answer/id #uuid "e73bbded-675f-57af-b332-48ee334c589c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700168}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9eca2ad-40bf-5527-8f7b-6d281edbce1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700161} :answer-field/id #uuid "c411b821-1658-505a-b73c-2243f33e7355" :answer-field/key "$\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F$ points in the positive $z$-direction everywhere" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700160} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "135ae37e-605b-5b69-8786-4bb553f776ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700120} {:answer/id #uuid "8801832a-b407-5662-bb76-efff078b27bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700144}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8801832a-b407-5662-bb76-efff078b27bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700144} :answer-field/id #uuid "e577d319-8411-5631-9220-02084c7c8494" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf F$ is irrotational" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700166} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a8a5964-1fa2-5ece-9b8f-c605556260eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700115} {:answer/id #uuid "a15ea9d2-3a1f-549c-ba25-d63540bc5022" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700149}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a8a5964-1fa2-5ece-9b8f-c605556260eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700115} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb6b34ae-c1ac-5ad4-9178-ec6200c3db3a" :answer-field/key "$\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F\\ne\\mathbf 0$ everywhere" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700177}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "203405d1-a80c-5438-8922-e7e548d07a52" :question/problem "![Vector field; arrows share one scale.](images/4e/4e9791f4cf71dae512cf952136a5c50e48d9ef03863b9f59d04d8c5109aeb785.png)\n\nThe diagram shows a vector field $\\mathbf F$ on $\\mathbb R^3$. Its $z$-component is zero and it is independent of $z$. View the $xy$-plane from the positive $z$-axis, so positive $z$ points out of the page. Both planar components are affine functions, and the displayed pattern continues throughout the domain.\n\n\n\nWhich statements are true everywhere? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Imagine a small paddlewheel with its axle parallel to the $z$-axis.\n\nThe horizontal flow is unchanged between the upper and lower sides of a wheel, so it contributes no rotation.\n\nThe vertical flow is unchanged between the right and left sides of a wheel, so it contributes no rotation.\n\nChanges of horizontal flow along the horizontal axis and vertical flow along the vertical axis stretch or compress the flow, but add no paddlewheel rotation.\n\nThe wheel does not spin. Thus $\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F=\\mathbf 0$ everywhere, and $\\mathbf F$ is **irrotational**. The zero vector has no direction.\n\n- $\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F\\ne\\mathbf 0$ everywhere: **false**.\n\n- $\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F$ points in the positive $z$-direction everywhere: **false**.\n\n- $\\mathbf F$ is irrotational: **true**.\n\n- $\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F=\\mathbf 0$ everywhere: **true**."}]}
